# Project Structure

GPUCloud Store is a localized marketing funnel: hero search → availability → use
cases → how-it-works → contact with plan (header Request Quote CTA). Product
intent lives in `README.md`; positioning notes in `docs/playbook.md`.

## Top-level layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `README.md` | Product overview, stack, env, scripts |
| `PLANNING.md` | Milestones, sequencing, coordination status board |
| `OPEN_ISSUES.md` | Current open work + acceptance criteria |
| `SCRATCHPAD.json` | Agent live session snapshot |
| `docs/` | Playbook + scoring/card design notes |
| `src/app/[locale]/` | App Router pages (home funnel under `(root)/(home)/`) |
| `src/components/` | Shared UI, forms, modals, layout-nav, consent |
| `src/components/ui/` | Primitives + visual effects (fog, streetlamp, morphing text) |
| `src/stores/` | Zustand stores (`plan`, `ui`) |
| `src/core/` | Domain models/schemas (e.g. `contact/`) |
| `src/server/` | Server actions + DB helpers |
| `src/lib/` | Hooks, plan helpers, templates, shared TS utilities |
| `src/i18n/` | next-intl wiring |
| `public/locales/` | Locale JSON (`en-US` source of truth) |
| `prisma/` | Optional persistence schema |
| `.cursor/rules/` | Agent workflow rules |

## Conventions

- Prefer extending existing funnel sections, stores, and form patterns over
  parallel systems.
- Keep **client UI** thin: validation/schemas and submit paths live in
  `src/core/` + `src/server/`; IO (email, CRM, DB) at the server edge.
- Plan identity and “needs configuration” logic belong in `src/stores/plan.ts`
  (and helpers under `src/lib/plan/`) — do not encode origin labels as identity.
- Locale keys: add to `public/locales/en-US.json` first; keep other locales in
  sync (or track lag in `OPEN_ISSUES.md`).
- Roadmap → `PLANNING.md`; concrete open work → `OPEN_ISSUES.md`; session memory →
  `SCRATCHPAD.json`. Do not use `README.md` as a task tracker.
- Heavy animations (fog, streetlamp, flickering cards) should eventually pause
  via the central viewport/links system — prefer that over ad-hoc observers.
